  "summary": "pypdf: Unvalidated JPEG image data loading",
  "description": "### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to arbitrary image parsers being called. This requires loading an image which claims to use the `/DCTDecode` filter (JPEG data).\n\nUsers which do not have the optional *Pillow* dependency installed in their environment are not affected.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.21.1](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.21.1).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#4222](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/4222).",
